Rust H.264 desktop encoder

The realtime encoder in crates/codec/kernels/h264 shares the existing LGPL-2.1-or-later
FFmpeg-derived interpolation, prediction, deblocking and CAVLC tables with the
decoder. Selected forward/inverse transform primitives retain the MIT attribution
from oxideav-h264 0.1.8 in the local syntax module. Frame decisions, motion search, rate control and
bitstream writing are implemented in the project. OpenH264 is not linked.

The specialized Rust encoder's GOM rate-control formulas, screen-change thresholds,
scroll detection, mode costs, quantization tables, residual decimation, prediction and motion-search
organization are adapted from Cisco OpenH264 source and verified
against UU's active producer/consumer paths. The original BSD-2-Clause notice is
retained in licenses/openh264-algorithms.txt. This attribution does not add the
OpenH264 C/C++ library or bindings to the application.


